# Candidate: retain the route union, move its execution to one server loader

Use `src/routes/[...path]/+page.server.ts` and `+page.svelte`. The existing `readDetailRoute(url.pathname)` already distinguishes root search, member/funder summary/history, and invalid paths, with checked IDs. Retaining it minimizes duplicated rules and keeps malformed paths in the existing not-found view. An explicit route tree is idiomatic but adds four wrappers and requires moving the same ID/view validation into parameter matchers. That buys little for this migration. Keep the catchall deliberately limited by the existing parser; it is never an API proxy.

The page server loader returns one serializable discriminated union:

```ts
type LoadedPage =
  | { kind: 'search'; query: string; strictness: number; result: SearchResult }
  | { kind: 'details'; route: EntityRoute; result: DetailResult }
  | { kind: 'not-found' };
type SearchResult =
  | { status: 'idle' }
  | { status: 'success'; term: string; entities: Entity[] }
  | { status: 'error'; term: string; message: string };
type EntityRoute = Extract<DetailRoute, { kind: 'member' | 'funder' }>;
type DetailResult = Exclude<DetailState, { kind: 'loading' }>;
```

`load` reads q/strictness, calls `depends('exposed:page')`, validates the pathname once, and dispatches to search/detail loading. It skips upstream search below the existing Unicode character minimum. Expected upstream failures become existing error cards; unknown routes and upstream 404s retain existing not-found markup and should carry HTTP 404. Keep loading state local to browser navigation rather than serializing an impossible completed-loader loading variant.

Module ownership:

- `lib/search.ts`: existing Entity and match source types, search configuration, readStrictness, labels, highlights, and pure entityHref(entity, searchParams).
- `lib/entity-details.ts`: existing detail types, route parser, formatting and summary helpers; make backToSearch(params), memberHref(id, view, params), funderHref(id, view, params) pure.
- `lib/server/search.ts`: current unknown-response parser and searchEntities({ term, strictness, fetch, signal }).
- `lib/server/entity-details.ts`: current detail parsers, identity consistency check and loadDetails({ route, fetch, signal }).
- `lib/server/api.ts`: private EXPOSED_API_ORIGIN from `$env/dynamic/private`, URL construction, and bounded fetch cancellation. Preserve meaningful existing error messages. Server-only code owns all wire response validation. Never return raw bodies or internal URLs in page data.
- `routes/+layout.svelte`: current global CSS/font imports and App shell. Use page pathname for skip-link choice or pass current route via page data. Delete main.ts, old index.html and obsolete App entry once migrated.
- `routes/[...path]/+page.svelte`: render SearchPage or EntityDetails using generated PageData.

SearchPage keeps the existing markup, debounce, IME flag, keyboard shortcuts and local raw query. Initialize from loader data, never window. Detect Mac shortcut on mount with a deterministic SSR fallback. Debounced input navigates through `goto(url, { replaceState: true, keepFocus: true, noScroll: true })`; same-URL retry calls invalidate('exposed:page'). Replacing history preserves the present search behavior. Composition suppresses navigation until compositionend. Short queries clear results immediately and update the Kit URL without upstream calls. Use Kit navigation APIs instead of native history.replaceState, which would discard Kit-owned history state.

Treat query/strictness as an input key. Only show loader results matching the current draft key. This matters when request A is in flight and the user starts composing or typing B before B's debounce fires. Kit supersedes navigations once B starts, but the key guard also covers the debounce window. An older completed loader must not overwrite the newer raw draft. Synchronize draft from page data on genuine back/forward navigation or entry from another route; preserve typed whitespace on self-initiated searches. Test this specifically. Search errors require retry even when the URL is unchanged. Detail retry invalidates the loader; route props/data remain reactive across member-to-member navigation.

Pass the current URL searchParams down to identity/declaration link builders or read `$app/state` only inside components. All shared helpers remain callable during SSR. Existing window references extend beyond App and SearchPage into entityHref/backToSearch, memberHref and funderHref, so migrating only top-level initialization is insufficient.

Use adapter-node with a production frontend Dockerfile that builds and runs `node build`. Remove Vite /api proxy completely. Compose publishes frontend only; remove exposed:6999 and postgres:55432 host port mappings under the strict reading of that requirement. Keep private service networking and EXPOSED_API_ORIGIN=http://exposed:6999. Dev frontend can retain its mounted Vite workflow, but production startup must be separately exercised against the adapter output.

Playwright page.route('/api/...') cannot intercept server-loader fetches. Replace those mocks with a local HTTP Rust-response stub and point EXPOSED_API_ORIGIN at it. Prefer one stub and frontend process per Playwright worker with distinct ports so test fixtures and retry counters cannot collide. If that is too much harness work, serialize tests against a single resettable stub; do not silently retain fullyParallel with shared mutable responses. Preserve assertions against upstream request URLs and payload validation.

Acceptance evidence: build and check; SSR HTML includes seeded search/detail content with JS disabled; browser live debounce, composition, retry, stale-response rejection, threshold and history tests pass; member/funder summary/history links retain q/strictness; invalid routes and missing entities display the existing view; browser network has no Rust-origin or /api calls; adapter-node works with the stub and Compose exposes frontend only. Capture desktop screenshots from the final running branch for the PR.
